module

public import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Chow.Bivariant.CommuteOverDedekindBase

/-!
# Proper pushforwards towards the base commute with bivariant classes over the base

Let `(S, δ)` be the base situation of chapter 42 of the Stacks Project, let `X` be a scheme
locally of finite type over `S`, let `π : X' ⟶ X` be proper and let `ξ ∈ A^p(X' ⟶ S)`. If
`c ∈ A^p(X ⟶ S)` is the proper pushforward `π_* ∘ ξ` of Stacks 0EPK and `ξ` commutes with
`c' ∈ A^q(Y ⟶ Z)` in the sense of `Stacks.Chow.BivariantCommuteOverBase`, then so does `c`. With
`Stacks.Chow.bivariantCommuteOverBase_of_isFlatPullbackOverBase` this widens Stacks 0FC6 from the
subgroup of `A^p(X ⟶ S)` generated by the flat-pullback operations towards the base to the
subgroup generated by those together with their proper pushforwards.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.Chow.testBaseChangeMapOfEq` — the base change `Y ×_Z T' ⟶ Y ×_Z T` of a morphism of
  test schemes over `Z`, formed at a morphism `T' ⟶ Z` presented as equal to the composite.
* `Stacks.Chow.mixedProperBaseChange` — the base change `Y ×_Z (X' ×_S T) ⟶ Y ×_Z (X ×_S T)` of
  the base change of `π` along a test scheme.
* `Stacks.Chow.chowOperationProperGenerators`,
  `Stacks.Chow.IsChowOperationProperGenerated` — the flat-pullback operations towards the base
  together with their proper pushforwards, and the subgroup of `A^p(X ⟶ S)` they generate.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Chow.BivariantClass.cap_properChowPushforward` — the proper-pushforward axiom of Stacks
  0B76 at a morphism of test schemes presented as equal to the composite rather than as the
  composite itself.
* `Stacks.Chow.mixedCommuteHom_comp_mixedProperBaseChange` — the comparison isomorphism of the
  two iterated fibre products is compatible with the two base changes of `π`.
* `Stacks.Chow.bivariantCommuteOverBase_of_isBivariantProperPushforward` — the proper-pushforward
  case of the proof of Stacks 0FC6.
* `Stacks.Chow.isChowOperationProperGenerated_of_isChowOperationGenerated` — the subgroup used
  here contains the subgroup of the flat-pullback operations alone.
* `Stacks.Chow.bivariantCommuteOverBase_of_isChowOperationProperGenerated` — **Stacks 0FC6** for a
  class `c` generated by the flat pullbacks towards the base and their proper pushforwards.

## Implementation notes

The presentation of a bivariant class towards a Dedekind base in the proof of Stacks 0FC5 is
`c = π_* ∘ ξ` for a proper `π : ⨿ X_i ⟶ X` and an integral combination `ξ = ∑ n_i ξ_i` whose terms
are flat pullbacks and Gysin maps. Each `X_i ⟶ X` is a closed immersion, hence proper, so once the
pushforward along `π` is decomposed into its pieces — which is not done here — a `c` of that shape
whose terms `ξ_i` are flat pullbacks is an integral combination of proper pushforwards of flat
pullbacks. The generators of that presentation covered here are therefore the flat pullbacks, the
proper pushforwards and the integral combinations, and the Gysin maps are not. Those are the
Gysin bivariant classes of Stacks 0B79 (`Stacks.Chow.gysinBivariantClass`), and they are not
generators here: a divisor chosen on `S` yields a module of the shape
`(pullback W).obj L`, whereas the Gysin axiom of Stacks 0B76 for `c'` needs
`(Scheme.Modules.pullback h).obj L_T`, and `Scheme.Modules.pullback` is only pseudofunctorial, so
the `chern` datum of a `Stacks.Chow.GysinSystem` relates the two Gysin maps not at all.

The identity to be proved compares `c' ∩ (ξ ∩ α)` on `Y ×_Z (X' ×_S T)`, where the test scheme
over `Z` is `pullback.snd (π ≫ sX) (t ≫ sZ) ≫ t`, with the proper-pushforward axiom of Stacks
0B76 for `c'`, where it is the composite of that base change of `π` with
`pullback.snd sX (t ≫ sZ) ≫ t`. These two morphisms are equal and not the same term, so their
fibre products with `Y ⟶ Z` are two objects; `Stacks.Chow.BivariantClass.cap_properChowPushforward`
states the axiom at either presentation, which removes the transport.

Stacks 02S1 and 02S2 are carried as hypotheses, in the shape of
`Stacks.Chow.FlatPullbackDescends` and `Stacks.Chow.ProperPushforwardDescends`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FC6](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FC6)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FC5](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FC5)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EPK](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EPK)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B76](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B76)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02R5](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02R5)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02S2](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02S2)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

universe u

namespace Stacks.Chow

/-! ### Base change of a morphism of test schemes at a presentation of the composite -/

section TestBaseChange

variable {Y Z T T' : Scheme.{u}} (w : Y ⟶ Z) (g : T ⟶ Z) (v : T' ⟶ T) (m : T' ⟶ Z)

/-- The base change `Y ×_Z T' ⟶ Y ×_Z T` of a morphism `v : T' ⟶ T` of test schemes over `Z`,
formed at a morphism `m : T' ⟶ Z` presented as equal to the composite `v ≫ g` rather than as that
composite itself. -/
def testBaseChangeMapOfEq (hm : v ≫ g = m) : pullback w m ⟶ pullback w g :=
  pullback.lift (pullback.fst w m) (pullback.snd w m ≫ v)
    (by rw [pullback.condition (f := w) (g := m), Category.assoc, hm])

/-- The base change `Y ×_Z T' ⟶ Y ×_Z T` commutes with the projections to `Y`. -/
@[reassoc (attr := simp)]
theorem testBaseChangeMapOfEq_fst (hm : v ≫ g = m) :
    testBaseChangeMapOfEq w g v m hm ≫ pullback.fst w g = pullback.fst w m :=
  pullback.lift_fst _ _ _

/-- The base change of `v : T' ⟶ T` followed by the projection to `T` is the projection to `T'`
followed by `v`. -/
@[reassoc (attr := simp)]
theorem testBaseChangeMapOfEq_snd (hm : v ≫ g = m) :
    testBaseChangeMapOfEq w g v m hm ≫ pullback.snd w g = pullback.snd w m ≫ v :=
  pullback.lift_snd _ _ _

/-- The base change of a morphism of test schemes sits in a cartesian square over it, the
vertical legs being the projections to the test schemes. -/
theorem isPullback_testBaseChangeMapOfEq (hm : v ≫ g = m) :
    IsPullback (pullback.snd w m) (testBaseChangeMapOfEq w g v m hm) v (pullback.snd w g) := by
  have hright : IsPullback (pullback.fst w g) (pullback.snd w g) w g :=
    IsPullback.of_hasPullback w g
  have key : ∀ (n : T' ⟶ Z), n = m → IsPullback (pullback.fst w m) (pullback.snd w m) w n := by
    intro n hn
    subst hn
    exact IsPullback.of_hasPullback _ _
  have hbig : IsPullback (testBaseChangeMapOfEq w g v m hm ≫ pullback.fst w g)
      (pullback.snd w m) w (v ≫ g) := by
    rw [testBaseChangeMapOfEq_fst]
    exact key (v ≫ g) hm
  exact (hbig.of_right (testBaseChangeMapOfEq_snd w g v m hm) hright).flip

/-- The base change of a proper morphism of test schemes is proper. -/
instance isProper_testBaseChangeMapOfEq [IsProper v] (hm : v ≫ g = m) :
    IsProper (testBaseChangeMapOfEq w g v m hm) :=
  MorphismProperty.of_isPullback (isPullback_testBaseChangeMapOfEq w g v m hm) (P := @IsProper)
    inferInstance

end TestBaseChange

/-! ### Transport of the proper-pushforward axiom to an equal test morphism -/

/-- **Stacks 0B76 (1).** The proper-pushforward axiom of a bivariant class at a morphism
`m : T' ⟶ Y` of test schemes presented as equal to the composite `h ≫ g` rather than as that
composite itself: the base change `h'` of `h` is then a morphism of the two fibre products as
they stand, and no transport along the equality is needed. -/
theorem BivariantClass.cap_properChowPushforward {C : ChowSituation.{u}} {G : GysinSystem C}
    {X Y : Scheme.{u}} {sX : X ⟶ C.S} [LocallyOfFiniteType sX] {sY : Y ⟶ C.S}
    [LocallyOfFiniteType sY] {f : X ⟶ Y} [LocallyOfFiniteType f] {hf : f ≫ sY = sX} {p : ℤ}
    (c : BivariantClass C G sX sY f hf p) (hpp : ProperPushforwardDescends C)
    {T T' : Scheme.{u}} (g : T ⟶ Y) [LocallyOfFiniteType g] (h : T' ⟶ T) [IsProper h]
    (m : T' ⟶ Y) [LocallyOfFiniteType m] (hm : h ≫ g = m)
    (h' : pullback f m ⟶ pullback f g) [IsProper h']
    (hfst : h' ≫ pullback.fst f g = pullback.fst f m)
    (hsnd : h' ≫ pullback.snd f g = pullback.snd f m ≫ h) (k : ℤ)
    (α : chowGroup C (m ≫ sY) k) :
    c.cap g k (properChowPushforward C (m ≫ sY) (g ≫ sY) h (by rw [← Category.assoc, hm]) k
        (hpp _ _ _ _ _) α) =
      properChowPushforward C (pullback.fst f m ≫ sX) (pullback.fst f g ≫ sX) h'
        (by rw [← Category.assoc, hfst]) (k - p) (hpp _ _ _ _ _) (c.cap m k α) := by
  subst hm
  have h'eq : h' = bivariantBaseChangeMap f g h := by
    refine pullback.hom_ext ?_ ?_
    · simp [hfst]
    · simp [hsnd]
  have sq : IsPullback (pullback.snd f (h ≫ g)) h' h (pullback.snd f g) := by
    rw [h'eq]
    exact isPullback_bivariantBaseChangeMap f g h
  exact c.proper_naturality g h h' sq hfst k (hpp _ _ _ _ _) (hpp _ _ _ _ _) α

/-! ### Pushforward across a commuting square with two isomorphism legs -/

/-- Pushing forward along a proper morphism and then along an isomorphism over the base agrees
with traversing a commuting square the other way. -/
theorem chowPushforwardOfIso_comm_properChowPushforward (C : ChowSituation.{u})
    {A B A' B' : Scheme.{u}} (sA : A ⟶ C.S) [LocallyOfFiniteType sA] (sB : B ⟶ C.S)
    [LocallyOfFiniteType sB] (sA' : A' ⟶ C.S) [LocallyOfFiniteType sA'] (sB' : B' ⟶ C.S)
    [LocallyOfFiniteType sB'] (vA : A ⟶ A') [IsIso vA] (vB : B ⟶ B') [IsIso vB] (uA : A ⟶ B)
    [IsProper uA] (uB : A' ⟶ B') [IsProper uB] (hsq : uA ≫ vB = vA ≫ uB)
    (hvA : vA ≫ sA' = sA) (hvB : vB ≫ sB' = sB) (huA : uA ≫ sB = sA) (huB : uB ≫ sB' = sA')
    (k : ℤ) (hfacA : ProperPushforwardFactorsThroughRationalEquivalence C sA sB uA huA k)
    (hfacB : ProperPushforwardFactorsThroughRationalEquivalence C sA' sB' uB huB k)
    (x : chowGroup C sA k) :
    chowPushforwardOfIso C sB sB' vB hvB k (properChowPushforward C sA sB uA huA k hfacA x) =
      properChowPushforward C sA' sB' uB huB k hfacB (chowPushforwardOfIso C sA sA' vA hvA k x) :=
  properChowPushforward_comp_eq C sA sB sA' sB' uA vB vA uB hsq huA hvB hvA huB k hfacA
    (properPushforwardFactorsThroughRationalEquivalence_of_isIso C sB sB' vB hvB k)
    (properPushforwardFactorsThroughRationalEquivalence_of_isIso C sA sA' vA hvA k) hfacB x

/-! ### The comparison isomorphism and a proper morphism towards the base -/

section MixedProper

variable {C : ChowSituation.{u}} {X X' Y Z : Scheme.{u}} (sX : X ⟶ C.S) (sZ : Z ⟶ C.S)
  (w : Y ⟶ Z) (π : X' ⟶ X)

/-- The base change `Y ×_Z (X' ×_S T) ⟶ Y ×_Z (X ×_S T)` along `Y ⟶ Z` of the base change
`X' ×_S T ⟶ X ×_S T` of `π` along a test scheme `t : T ⟶ Z`. -/
def mixedProperBaseChange {T : Scheme.{u}} (t : T ⟶ Z) :
    pullback w (pullback.snd (π ≫ sX) (t ≫ sZ) ≫ t) ⟶
      pullback w (pullback.snd sX (t ≫ sZ) ≫ t) :=
  testBaseChangeMapOfEq w (pullback.snd sX (t ≫ sZ) ≫ t)
    (bivariantPushforwardBaseChange π sX (t ≫ sZ)) (pullback.snd (π ≫ sX) (t ≫ sZ) ≫ t)
    (by rw [← Category.assoc, bivariantPushforwardBaseChange_snd])

/-- The base change of `π` on the iterated fibre product commutes with the projections to `Y`. -/
@[reassoc (attr := simp)]
theorem mixedProperBaseChange_fst {T : Scheme.{u}} (t : T ⟶ Z) :
    mixedProperBaseChange sX sZ w π t ≫ pullback.fst w (pullback.snd sX (t ≫ sZ) ≫ t) =
      pullback.fst w (pullback.snd (π ≫ sX) (t ≫ sZ) ≫ t) :=
  testBaseChangeMapOfEq_fst _ _ _ _ _

/-- The base change of `π` on the iterated fibre product followed by the projection to
`X ×_S T` is the projection to `X' ×_S T` followed by the base change `X' ×_S T ⟶ X ×_S T` of
`π`. -/
@[reassoc (attr := simp)]
theorem mixedProperBaseChange_snd {T : Scheme.{u}} (t : T ⟶ Z) :
    mixedProperBaseChange sX sZ w π t ≫ pullback.snd w (pullback.snd sX (t ≫ sZ) ≫ t) =
      pullback.snd w (pullback.snd (π ≫ sX) (t ≫ sZ) ≫ t) ≫
        bivariantPushforwardBaseChange π sX (t ≫ sZ) :=
  testBaseChangeMapOfEq_snd _ _ _ _ _

/-- The base change of a proper `π` on the iterated fibre product is proper. -/
instance isProper_mixedProperBaseChange [IsProper π] {T : Scheme.{u}} (t : T ⟶ Z) :
    IsProper (mixedProperBaseChange sX sZ w π t) :=
  isProper_testBaseChangeMapOfEq _ _ _ _ _

/-- The base change of `π` on the iterated fibre product is a morphism over the base. -/
theorem mixedProperBaseChange_comp_structureMorphism {T : Scheme.{u}} (t : T ⟶ Z) :
    mixedProperBaseChange sX sZ w π t ≫
        (pullback.fst w (pullback.snd sX (t ≫ sZ) ≫ t) ≫ (w ≫ sZ)) =
      pullback.fst w (pullback.snd (π ≫ sX) (t ≫ sZ) ≫ t) ≫ (w ≫ sZ) := by
  rw [← Category.assoc, mixedProperBaseChange_fst]

/-- The comparison isomorphism of the two iterated fibre products is compatible with the two base
changes of a morphism `π : X' ⟶ X` over the base. -/
theorem mixedCommuteHom_comp_mixedProperBaseChange {T : Scheme.{u}} (t : T ⟶ Z) :
    mixedCommuteHom (π ≫ sX) sZ w t ≫ mixedProperBaseChange sX sZ w π t =
      bivariantPushforwardBaseChange π sX (pullback.fst w t ≫ (w ≫ sZ)) ≫
        mixedCommuteHom sX sZ w t := by
  refine pullback.hom_ext ?_ (pullback.hom_ext ?_ ?_) <;> simp

end MixedProper

/-! ### The proper-pushforward case of Stacks 0FC6 -/

section Main

variable (C : ChowSituation.{u}) (G : GysinSystem C) {X X' Y Z : Scheme.{u}} (sX : X ⟶ C.S)
  [LocallyOfFiniteType sX] (sZ : Z ⟶ C.S) [LocallyOfFiniteType sZ] (w : Y ⟶ Z)
  [LocallyOfFiniteType w] (π : X' ⟶ X) [IsProper π] (hpp : ProperPushforwardDescends C) (p q : ℤ)
  (c : BivariantClass C G sX (𝟙 C.S) sX (Category.comp_id sX) p)
  (ξ : BivariantClass C G (π ≫ sX) (𝟙 C.S) (π ≫ sX) (Category.comp_id (π ≫ sX)) p)
  (c' : BivariantClass C G (w ≫ sZ) sZ w rfl q)

/-- The proper pushforward of Stacks 0EPK of a class towards the base which commutes with `c'`
commutes with `c'`. This is the proper-pushforward case of the proof of Stacks 0FC6: the identity
to be proved is the proper-pushforward axiom of Stacks 0B76 for `c'`, read through the comparison
isomorphism of the two iterated fibre products. -/
theorem bivariantCommuteOverBase_of_isBivariantProperPushforward
    (hξ : IsBivariantProperPushforward C G (π ≫ sX) sX (𝟙 C.S) π sX rfl (Category.comp_id sX)
      hpp p ξ c)
    (hcomm : BivariantCommuteOverBase C G (π ≫ sX) sZ w p q ξ c') :
    BivariantCommuteOverBase C G sX sZ w p q c c' := by
  intro T t _ k α
  have hVT : bivariantPushforwardBaseChange π sX (t ≫ sZ) ≫ (pullback.snd sX (t ≫ sZ) ≫ t) =
      pullback.snd (π ≫ sX) (t ≫ sZ) ≫ t := by
    rw [← Category.assoc, bivariantPushforwardBaseChange_snd]
  have eT : ∀ {A : Scheme.{u}} (s : A ⟶ C.S),
      pullback.fst s (t ≫ sZ) ≫ s = (pullback.snd s (t ≫ sZ) ≫ t) ≫ sZ := fun s ↦ by
    rw [Category.assoc]
    exact pullback.condition
  have hstr := fun {T' : Scheme.{u}} (u : T' ⟶ C.S) ↦
    bivariantPushforwardBaseChange_comp_structure (rfl : π ≫ sX = π ≫ sX) sX u
  have hVTbase : bivariantPushforwardBaseChange π sX (t ≫ sZ) ≫
      ((pullback.snd sX (t ≫ sZ) ≫ t) ≫ sZ) = (pullback.snd (π ≫ sX) (t ≫ sZ) ≫ t) ≫ sZ := by
    rw [← Category.assoc, hVT]
  have key := hcomm t k α
  simp only [mixedIteratedCapBaseFirst_apply, mixedIteratedCapBaseLast_apply] at key ⊢
  rw [hξ (pullback.fst w t ≫ (w ≫ sZ)) (k - q) _, hξ (t ≫ sZ) k _,
    bivariantProperPushforwardCap_apply, bivariantProperPushforwardCap_apply,
    chowPushforwardOfIso_comm_properChowPushforward C
      (pullback.fst (π ≫ sX) (pullback.fst w t ≫ (w ≫ sZ)) ≫ (π ≫ sX))
      (pullback.fst sX (pullback.fst w t ≫ (w ≫ sZ)) ≫ sX)
      (pullback.fst w (pullback.snd (π ≫ sX) (t ≫ sZ) ≫ t) ≫ (w ≫ sZ))
      (pullback.fst w (pullback.snd sX (t ≫ sZ) ≫ t) ≫ (w ≫ sZ))
      (mixedCommuteHom (π ≫ sX) sZ w t) (mixedCommuteHom sX sZ w t)
      (bivariantPushforwardBaseChange π sX (pullback.fst w t ≫ (w ≫ sZ)))
      (mixedProperBaseChange sX sZ w π t)
      (mixedCommuteHom_comp_mixedProperBaseChange sX sZ w π t).symm
      (mixedCommuteHom_comp_structureMorphism (π ≫ sX) sZ w t)
      (mixedCommuteHom_comp_structureMorphism sX sZ w t) (hstr _)
      (mixedProperBaseChange_comp_structureMorphism sX sZ w π t) ((k - q) - p)
      (hpp _ _ _ _ _) (hpp _ _ _ _ _) _,
    key,
    properChowPushforward_chowGroupCongr C (eT _) (eT _)
      (bivariantPushforwardBaseChange π sX (t ≫ sZ)) (hstr _) hVTbase (k - p)
      (hpp _ _ _ _ _) (hpp _ _ _ _ _) _,
    BivariantClass.cap_properChowPushforward c' hpp (pullback.snd sX (t ≫ sZ) ≫ t)
      (bivariantPushforwardBaseChange π sX (t ≫ sZ))
      (pullback.snd (π ≫ sX) (t ≫ sZ) ≫ t) hVT (mixedProperBaseChange sX sZ w π t)
      (mixedProperBaseChange_fst sX sZ w π t) (mixedProperBaseChange_snd sX sZ w π t) (k - p) _]
  refine eq_of_heq (HEq.trans ?_ (HEq.symm (chowGroupDegreeEquiv_heq C
    (pullback.fst w (pullback.snd sX (t ≫ sZ) ≫ t) ≫ (w ≫ sZ)) _ _)))
  exact heq_map_index (by ring) (chowGroupDegreeEquiv_heq C
    (pullback.fst w (pullback.snd (π ≫ sX) (t ≫ sZ) ≫ t) ≫ (w ≫ sZ)) _ _)
    (fun n y ↦ properChowPushforward C
      (pullback.fst w (pullback.snd (π ≫ sX) (t ≫ sZ) ≫ t) ≫ (w ≫ sZ))
      (pullback.fst w (pullback.snd sX (t ≫ sZ) ≫ t) ≫ (w ≫ sZ))
      (mixedProperBaseChange sX sZ w π t)
      (mixedProperBaseChange_comp_structureMorphism sX sZ w π t) n (hpp _ _ _ _ _) y)

end Main

/-! ### Classes generated by the operations of chapter 42 with proper pushforward -/

/-- The flat-pullback operations towards the base together with their proper pushforwards along
proper morphisms over the base: the generators, among the operations available in this repository,
of the presentation of a bivariant class towards a Dedekind base established in the proof of
Stacks 0FC5. That presentation also uses Gysin maps, whose bivariant classes
(`Stacks.Chow.gysinBivariantClass`, Stacks 0B79) are not among these generators. -/
def chowOperationProperGenerators (C : ChowSituation.{u}) (G : GysinSystem C)
    (hpp : ProperPushforwardDescends C) {X : Scheme.{u}} (sX : X ⟶ C.S)
    [LocallyOfFiniteType sX] (p : ℤ) :
    Set (BivariantClass C G sX (𝟙 C.S) sX (Category.comp_id sX) p) :=
  chowOperationGenerators C G sX p ∪
    {c | ∃ (X' : Scheme.{u}) (π : X' ⟶ X) (_hπ : IsProper π)
      (ξ : BivariantClass C G (π ≫ sX) (𝟙 C.S) (π ≫ sX) (Category.comp_id (π ≫ sX)) p),
      IsChowOperationGenerated C G (π ≫ sX) p ξ ∧
        IsBivariantProperPushforward C G (π ≫ sX) sX (𝟙 C.S) π sX rfl (Category.comp_id sX)
          hpp p ξ c}

/-- The assertion that `c ∈ A^p(X ⟶ S)` is a `ℤ`-linear combination of flat-pullback operations
towards the base and of proper pushforwards of such combinations. -/
def IsChowOperationProperGenerated (C : ChowSituation.{u}) (G : GysinSystem C)
    (hpp : ProperPushforwardDescends C) {X : Scheme.{u}} (sX : X ⟶ C.S)
    [LocallyOfFiniteType sX] (p : ℤ)
    (c : BivariantClass C G sX (𝟙 C.S) sX (Category.comp_id sX) p) : Prop :=
  c ∈ AddSubgroup.closure (chowOperationProperGenerators C G hpp sX p)

/-- Every combination of flat-pullback operations towards the base is one of those operations
together with their proper pushforwards, so the subgroup of
`Stacks.Chow.IsChowOperationProperGenerated` contains the one of
`Stacks.Chow.IsChowOperationGenerated`. -/
theorem isChowOperationProperGenerated_of_isChowOperationGenerated (C : ChowSituation.{u})
    (G : GysinSystem C) (hpp : ProperPushforwardDescends C) {X : Scheme.{u}} (sX : X ⟶ C.S)
    [LocallyOfFiniteType sX] (p : ℤ)
    {c : BivariantClass C G sX (𝟙 C.S) sX (Category.comp_id sX) p}
    (hc : IsChowOperationGenerated C G sX p c) :
    IsChowOperationProperGenerated C G hpp sX p c :=
  AddSubgroup.closure_mono Set.subset_union_left hc

section Widened

variable (C : ChowSituation.{u}) (G : GysinSystem C) {X Y Z : Scheme.{u}} (sX : X ⟶ C.S)
  [LocallyOfFiniteType sX] (sZ : Z ⟶ C.S) [LocallyOfFiniteType sZ] (w : Y ⟶ Z)
  [LocallyOfFiniteType w] (hpp : ProperPushforwardDescends C) (p q : ℤ)
  (c : BivariantClass C G sX (𝟙 C.S) sX (Category.comp_id sX) p)
  (c' : BivariantClass C G (w ≫ sZ) sZ w rfl q)

/-- **Stacks 0FC6.** Let `(S, δ)` be as in Stacks section 42.63, let `X` be a scheme locally of
finite type over `S` and let `c ∈ A^p(X ⟶ S)`. Let `Y ⟶ Z` be a morphism of schemes locally of
finite type over `S` and let `c' ∈ A^q(Y ⟶ Z)`. Then `c ∘ c' = c' ∘ c`: capping with `c` and
capping with `c'` may be performed in either order, the two results being read on the two
iterated fibre products `X ×_S (Y ×_Z T)` and `Y ×_Z (X ×_S T)` of a test scheme through the
canonical comparison isomorphism. -/
@[stacks 0FC6 "the commutation c ∘ c' = c' ∘ c, read on the cap operations of the two \
composites, for a c in the subgroup of A^p(X ⟶ S) generated by the flat pullbacks towards the \
base and by their proper pushforwards: of the generators the proof of Stacks 0FC5 exhibits this \
covers flat pullback, proper pushforward and integral combinations and not the Gysin maps; \
given Stacks 02S1 for flat and 02S2 for proper maps over the base"]
theorem bivariantCommuteOverBase_of_isChowOperationProperGenerated
    (hfd : ∀ {A B : Scheme.{u}} (sA : A ⟶ C.S) [LocallyOfFiniteType sA]
      (sB : B ⟶ C.S) [LocallyOfFiniteType sB] (v : A ⟶ B) [LocallyOfFiniteType v] [Flat v]
      (hv : v ≫ sB = sA) (r : ℕ) (hr : AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeDimension v r) (k : ℤ),
      FlatPullbackFactorsThroughRationalEquivalence C sA sB v hv r hr k)
    (hgen : IsChowOperationProperGenerated C G hpp sX p c) :
    BivariantCommuteOverBase C G sX sZ w p q c c' := by
  refine AddSubgroup.closure_induction
    (p := fun x _ ↦ BivariantCommuteOverBase C G sX sZ w p q x c') ?_ ?_ ?_ ?_ hgen
  · rintro x (⟨r, hflat, hp, hrX, hx⟩ | ⟨X', π, hπ, ξ, hgenξ, hpf⟩)
    · have : Flat sX := hflat
      intro T t _ k α
      exact bivariantCommuteOverBase_of_isFlatPullbackOverBase C G sX sZ w r p q x c' hfd hp hrX
        hx t k α
    · have : IsProper π := hπ
      intro T t _ k α
      exact bivariantCommuteOverBase_of_isBivariantProperPushforward C G sX sZ w π hpp p q x ξ c'
        hpf (bivariantCommuteOverBase_of_isChowOperationGenerated C G (π ≫ sX) sZ w p q ξ c' hfd
          hgenξ) t k α
  · intro T t _ k α
    exact bivariantCommuteOverBase_zero C G sX sZ w p q c' t k α
  · intro x y _ _ hx hy T t _ k α
    exact bivariantCommuteOverBase_add C G sX sZ w p q c' hx hy t k α
  · intro x _ hx T t _ k α
    exact bivariantCommuteOverBase_neg C G sX sZ w p q c' hx t k α

end Widened

end Stacks.Chow

